{"name":"Belize","hex":"#7fd3d3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Belize","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An English-speaking country in Central America, formerly called British Honduras."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Belize"}],"entries":[{"title":"Belize","blocks":[{"text":"Belize is a country on the north-eastern coast of Central America. It is bordered by Mexico to the north, the Caribbean Sea to the east, and Guatemala to the west and south. It also shares a maritime boundary with Honduras to the southeast. Part of the Caribbean region, Belize is a member of the Caribbean Community (CARICOM) and the Commonwealth Caribbean, the historical British West Indies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Flag_of_Belize.svg/330px-Flag_of_Belize.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belize","wikidata":"Q242"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/St._George%27s_Cay_Day_Official_Holiday.jpg/500px-St._George%27s_Cay_Day_Official_Holiday.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/St._George%27s_Cay_Day_Official_Holiday.jpg/500px-St._George%27s_Cay_Day_Official_Holiday.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An excerpt from the 1898 Gazette that declared 10 September an official holiday, Battle of St. George's Caye Day","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt._George's_Cay_Day_Official_Holiday.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/British_Honduras_1962_Hurricane_Hattie_stamp.jpg/500px-British_Honduras_1962_Hurricane_Hattie_stamp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/British_Honduras_1